/ref 17592186195295} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3da49fe-cd31-5fd0-8080-5adaa06a3c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195302} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b6568d-f33b-5a67-a639-e25a73c6472e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195303} {:answer/id #uuid "d8462882-ac97-55db-b842-ee581253a25a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195304} {:answer/id #uuid "659d0c66-c6a1-5d99-83a7-4cf082d72c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195305} {:answer/id #uuid "70276463-1f0d-52c2-8769-bd6cbd778d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70276463-1f0d-52c2-8769-bd6cbd778d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195306} :answer-field/id #uuid "455c0b8c-6444-5429-b6db-d77d9acb4a25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "576083d0-69bc-5a44-8497-3c93280947cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-181600" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/assets/83ebd6f5d742a869b267a0cead4a9a94ae17fa534ca3e1cfddbb495c67390ecf.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-x\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x$ and *below* the line $y=2.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x,\\,y<2.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-x<y<2.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=-x$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n-x\\le y<2\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x\\le y<2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36fa0f2f-3812-521a-aca3-900556be84ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Non-Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ca276ea-f25a-5a0d-b4e2-f54ee1550527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324139} {:answer/id #uuid "af7ab909-5668-5be9-9bcc-3f71e8264e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ca276ea-f25a-5a0d-b4e2-f54ee1550527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324139} :answer-field/id #uuid "44750a13-f5d9-5ed1-ba24-90bf45e702b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f510c544-28bc-5a4f-9019-dae6f270165d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f510c544-28bc-5a4f-9019-dae6f270165d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324142} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca2f83ff-acd0-5c85-8a25-55554d6da5ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9514b47-883b-5f75-8351-7bda7ce95975" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9514b47-883b-5f75-8351-7bda7ce95975" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324144} :answer-field/id #uuid "78a507d8-3547-5d06-9532-b0c9abda6de8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b4e1ca48-5085-5e98-9dc5-2438b5edfafe" :question/math-academy-id "q-181694" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/assets/c670ed592fc32716596aae470911923627d1c6861a75a1c885659d09005e0a84.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n${y}^{2}$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$36$\n\n$}$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the elliptical boundary of our region has horizontal radius $a=2$ and vertical radius $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in describing all points that lie *inside* the ellipse. So, let's pick any point inside the region, say, $(0,0).$ Substituting its coordinates into the equation of the boundary, we obtain\n\n$$\n9(0)^{2}+4(0)^{2}\\,<\\,36.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the points $P(x,y)$ in our region are any real numbers that satisfy the condition\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the curve $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 36.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 36}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e694b201-5ec6-5cc3-a608-2447d1cc1ed3" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, One Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc636fc0-a884-5e6f-8e2f-eb0acc20b395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324147} {:answer/id #uuid "61da26c7-e591-5968-b270-3b14d8b86c1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324148} {:answer/id #uuid "e4895942-3164-5d01-80ce-c091c763efd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324149} {:answer/id #uuid "86001284-c8ed-50a8-b244-67de7558bd6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc636fc0-a884-5e6f-8e2f-eb0acc20b395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324147} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8221f01-9849-5913-806f-8febfb7e471a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324146} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2097b00-767f-5bff-95fd-fd4930c136eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324152} {:answer/id #uuid "20b2e153-620f-59e4-8ad3-a460360b09cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324153} {:answer/id #uuid "2516579d-f799-5469-9219-501aedf376e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324154} {:answer/id #uuid "460564f2-983f-5125-8729-a24cf9be84c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324155} {:answer/id #uuid "f59aa6eb-eceb-522c-85d4-aaef9a5dca18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2097b00-767f-5bff-95fd-fd4930c136eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324152} :answer-field/id #uuid "7444df0c-3405-58f5-9a5b-29232e48d378" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6966f4d8-cdcd-5ca4-b362-30814d3591d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-181999" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/assets/c7f7b1dc9bf4da61b573345aaf92fe0d29ea00ef5558a9fca985d8af25fa0a03.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\ny>2.\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e694b201-5ec6-5cc3-a608-2447d1cc1ed3" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, One Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ccef57f-a6ae-5d6e-8b8e-7c40e3d9356a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324159} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd2743d-d43b-5e2d-b01c-a07dfd8dafd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324160} {:answer/id #uuid "539f7f21-2636-5730-9734-ea6bd57b3454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324161} {:answer/id #uuid "7de7d061-8fa0-5d88-adaa-0678a6c7dba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324162} {:answer/id #uuid "b13e9150-340b-5b5c-9106-e69a19861d7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324163} {:answer/id #uuid "85798dd3-a868-5c62-94a9-4ea01e560c77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7de7d061-8fa0-5d88-adaa-0678a6c7dba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324162} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff26241f-131f-5db2-8b74-8136257a631e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324158} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e1c3090-2fec-5d29-984d-0bf9fb667137" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324166} {:answer/id #uuid "ee56cfac-6fcb-5c2d-a62e-18363d679b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324167} {:answer/id #uuid "9b3e7c67-83c4-5478-a1b7-907eae2356d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324168} {:answer/id #uuid "414a2074-48e8-5e5c-89a1-eb2f7b356a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324169} {:answer/id #uuid "9e8b35eb-c6e0-5077-b16b-7822d67bdc59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "414a2074-48e8-5e5c-89a1-eb2f7b356a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324169} :answer-field/id #uuid "a634d752-80a2-53bf-b41d-83d6262fc1f0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3a75647-b6f0-514a-9eb0-d39182f0d5fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-182016" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044982/assets/f54c771d1b7045bbaa301c9d595a45dc64fbdfc6b1c83c152fb6fc892373ea06.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,-1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-1.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-1\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that some points in our set lie *on* the line. We include these points by changing the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\ge -1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -1}\n$$"}]}
